# Live Caddy site for serving the BAM Store repository over the tailnet.
#
# This is managed through the `caddyedit` Record API (see the `caddy` skill), not
# hand-edited — the block below documents what that record installs into
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile:
#
#     apps.bam:80 {
#         root * /data/bam-store/repo
#         file_server
#     }
#
# Plain HTTP is intentional: everything is reached over Tailscale, which already
# encrypts and authenticates the connection, so TLS would just re-wrap an
# encrypted tunnel. The client's default base URL is http://apps.bam/.
#
# No bearer token is set — access is limited to the tailnet by Tailscale ACLs. If
# you later want per-app gating, add a matcher that checks
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and have the client send the same token.
